@airMeng Added `test/registered/xpu/llm_models/test_xpu_glm_4_7_flash.py` in 3b5b2618ad: GLM-4.7-Flash GSM8K on XPU at TP=4, in the `nightly-xpu-kernel-main-4-gpu` suite with the same mixin as the Qwen3-30B-A3B test. No existing test covers this path; the other GLM-4.7-Flash tests are CUDA only or CPU unit tests of the gate.

On Arc Pro B60 (main 6e667c4310 plus this fix) it scores 0.96 on its 50 questions against a threshold of 0.90, in 1431 s. With the factor applied twice the model scores about 0.25. `--max-running-requests 4` is the B60 setting that keeps concurrent requests from losing the device.

Could you take it into the next weekly consolidation ?

